    <!-- Winged Victory of Samothrace as line work, framed exactly where
         ic_winged_victory frames it, so the themed launcher icon and the coloured one
         are the same statue at the same size. Drawn rather than filled: a themed icon
         is a single flat colour, and a solid silhouette at that size is a blob with the
         wing feathers and the drapery folds lost inside it — the lines are the only
         thing left that can carry them.

         Both the weight and the amount of detail are set for the size this is really
         drawn at, which is small in every use and large in none: a themed home-screen
         icon gives the monochrome layer around 28dp once its inset is taken, and the
         status bar draws the notification's copy at 24 by 38 pixels on a 420dpi phone.
         So the tracing's own half-unit lines are stroked up to about six units, and
         most of its contours are dropped — at this weight neighbouring lines close up
         into the blob the drawing exists to avoid.

         What is dropped is chosen by where a line is and what it does, not by its
         length alone. Length alone deletes the statue: its outline is traced as a
         run of medium-length pieces rather than one long one, so a threshold high
         enough to clear the drapery takes the skirt's own edge with it and leaves a
         wing hanging over scribbles. The outline is therefore identified first — the
         ink is closed over the gaps between strokes and filled from the outside in,
         and every contour lying along that edge is kept whatever its length, 52 of
         them below the smallest threshold here. Only the interior is thinned, and by
         region: the wing keeps everything above 30 units of perimeter because feathers
         are what the shape is recognised by, the head and torso 60, the hip 80, and
         the skirt 110, where folds cost more than they say. -->
